From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] rotation-manager: keep a locked orientation on lock and unlock

On phones phosh rotates the lock screen to portrait and restores the
pre-lock transform on unlock.  With the Pro1X keyboard slid out the
orientation is locked in landscape; the session starts locked, so the
saved pre-lock transform was portrait and unlocking turned the shell
to portrait with the keyboard out.  When the orientation is locked,
leave the transform alone (the landscape lock screen works at this
panel size).  phosh 0.56.0.
---
--- a/src/rotation-manager.c
+++ b/src/rotation-manager.c
@@ -262,6 +262,14 @@
   if (!is_phone (self))
     return;
 
+  /* Orientation locked (on the Pro1X: keyboard slid out, landscape):
+   * keep the current orientation for the lock screen, and do not
+   * restore an older one on unlock. */
+  if (self->orientation_locked) {
+    self->prelock_transform = -1;
+    return;
+  }
+
   /* Don't mess with transforms on external screens either */
   if (!phosh_monitor_is_builtin (self->monitor))
     return;
